Changes made in this fork (2026, by PeytonG; see the git history for detail):
- Renamed the app to Meadhall, with new artwork, a pixel-art look, a bright purple
  default theme and a pixel color wheel for choosing the theme color.
- Voice channels use MatrixRTC so they interoperate with Element Call, including
  end-to-end encrypted media; heorot-voice-relay is kept as a fallback.
- Voice channels let members join calls (call membership power level); the
  Discord import no longer breaks power levels for restricted channels.
- Desktop: auto-updates from GitHub Releases, tray icon, open at login, and a
  permission handler restricting renderer permissions to the app.
- Typecheck fix, and unit, smoke, Synapse integration and Playwright E2E tests
  with GitHub Actions CI.
- Release builds (Windows, Linux, Android), security scanning and documentation.
- Discord-style Home (direct messages and group chats) and a one-screen phone
  layout; calls in DMs and group chats; mute/deafen outside calls; per-person
  volume up to 120%; a voice changer; a font picker; round profile pictures;
  registration tokens on sign-up; homeserver discovery before signing in.
- Discord-style roles and permissions mapped onto Matrix power levels; a server
  admin panel (Synapse Admin API); incoming-call ringtone; pixel emoji; speaking
  campfire; desktop and Android background notifications (no Google services).
- Status (Away, Do Not Disturb, Invisible, custom status, automatic Away, a phone
  icon, "Playing ..." from Steam); profiles with banners, bios, links and roles;
  per-channel "who can talk"; a desktop tray menu; several signed-in accounts with
  notifications for all; a soundboard with synthesized sounds and more voice
  effects; a high contrast theme; update notices on phones and "What's new" after
  updates; an iOS project (Capacitor) with a Codemagic build.

